  "text": "Mary ignored the whole room and chose the moment. Luke chapter ten. Jesus comes into a village, and a woman named Martha receives him into her house. Her sister Mary sits down at his feet and listens to what he is saying. And Martha is cumbered about much serving. The word carries the sense of being pulled in every direction. She is doing real work, and nobody is helping, and eventually she does what a lot of us do. She takes it to Jesus and makes it his problem. Lord, dost thou not care that my sister hath left me to serve alone? Bid her therefore that she help me. And she is not wrong that she is alone. Look at his answer, because it is gentler than people make it sound. Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things. He says her name twice. That is not a scolding, that is tenderness. But one thing is needful, and Mary hath chosen that good part, which shall not be taken away from her. He does not tell Mary to get up. He tells Martha she is allowed to sit down.",
